```python
def recursive_linear_search(numbers, target):
    def search(numbers, target, index):
        if index == len(numbers):
            return -1
        if numbers[index] == target:
            return index
        return search(numbers, target, index + 1)

    return search(numbers, target, 0)
```

This algorithm utilizes a recursive approach to check each number in the list until the target number is found or the end of the list is reached. The time complexity of this algorithm is O(n) because in the worst case scenario, it needs to check each element in the list once.

